{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-projective}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:042bd14146df96d15604925dd7bbc94d133023c03ab695e31372481af4e84255", "source_text": "Projective morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93c7b36e5dbe83b8acb2c31e9a53b03a1986577516de31f64dc0a040613ad3a9", "unit_id": "tag:01W7:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\cite{EGA}", "REF_0002": "\\cite{H}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bdbb3e073cfd024457b2790978c653e55821580fe6f4f9c2d926f81978d560dc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will use the definition of a projective morphism from <REF_0001>.\nThe version of the definition with the ``H'' is the one\nfrom <REF_0002>. The resulting definitions are different. Both are useful.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:839ddbce80191dfe6bff48924dee84108af824e88cb7e8b455b06279275ddbc7", "unit_id": "tag:01W7:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathbf{P}(\\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{E}$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$n$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\to \\mathbf{P}^n_S$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$f$", "MATH_0013": "$S = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0014": "$f^{-1}(U_i) \\to U_i$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-projective}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf1cef857c215b9aebe3ef7bd87f7fd11cc8a313a0e6f0f006612a40524e048f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:746ad854e8c4f427a8c3dae584f0a4cc7f4cc9b24b1c3a369d2dc0f1ab485a30", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0003> is isomorphic as\nan <MATH_0004>-scheme to a closed subscheme of a projective\nbundle <MATH_0005>\nfor some quasi-coherent, finite type <MATH_0006>-module <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0008> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>H-projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if there exists an integer <MATH_0009> and\na closed immersion <MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0004> We say <MATH_0012> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>locally projective<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if there exists an open\ncovering <MATH_0013> such that each <MATH_0014> is\nprojective.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81496b173ee29fe3a259a6ccdd539f94198a16eafef108fda0fe8d160ed17193", "unit_id": "tag:01W8:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01W7", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-projective-quasi-projective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-projective-open-projective}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-projective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:89c7b0c123faa6821acd52e127d9b087b12ad0577647e47cdcd7d3afb809f7fc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAs expected, a projective morphism is quasi-projective, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nConversely, quasi-projective morphisms are often compositions\nof open immersions and projective morphisms, see\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nFor an overview of properties of projective morphisms over\na quasi-projective base, see\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:114daa117fed97e7018f663569aefbab10650b865b69d5467e8f5e30e6a50abb", "unit_id": "tag:01W7:prose-0002"}
